  "id": "matching-to-sample",
  "term": "matching to sample",
  "definition": "Matching to sample is a learning task in which one stimulus is presented first and the subject must then pick the identical or corresponding stimulus from two options to receive a reward. It is used to assess whether the subject can learn and apply a matching rule, including with abstract cues.",
